RAM-refund variant of the radix-4 fusion (a800d1ea1896): NOT a primary repeat. It carries the fusion's 5.1467 speed claim but its purpose is the heap: off-device nm/size show .iram0.text 73,551 -> 72,435 (-1,116 B), which is more than the 1,024 B the fusion itself costs, so the fusion could ship at a net internal-RAM gain over the accepted 12,855. This session measures internal_free, think_tps and boot_bench on the image, which is what decides whether the cost objection to the fusion is retired. Restricted groups (primary,think), so the device byte-exact gate is skipped by design and this is not an acceptance attempt.
